# =============================================================================
# ui/.dockerignore
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose:
#   Excludes from the ui/ build context everything ui/Dockerfile does not COPY,
#   so the daemon never receives it.
#
# Governing convention:
#   docs/CODE_DOCUMENTATION_STANDARD.md
#
# Assumptions: this file is required rather than tidy-minded. node_modules is a
#   283 MB tree of host-resolved, possibly host-native packages, and dist is a
#   previous local build; either one sent into the context would be uploaded on
#   every build and, worse, dist would be shadowed by a stale copy if a future
#   instruction ever copied the whole directory. The Dockerfile names its inputs
#   explicitly, so nothing here is load-bearing for correctness today -- it is the
#   guard that keeps that true when an instruction is added.
# Trade-offs: the list names paths rather than using a deny-all-then-allow shape.
#   A deny-all list is stricter but makes every new source directory an invisible
#   omission at build time, whereas an over-broad context is merely slower.
# =============================================================================

node_modules
dist
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
